Once upon a time in the dense jungles of Stranglethorn Vale, a Gnome Warlock named Zappo quested alongside his Succubus pet. They roamed the land, facing various challenges. The Succubus, with her alluring charm, often mesmerized enemies, making them easier to defeat. However, when facing a particularly tough group of enemies, Zappo found himself in a tight spot. The Succubus's Seduction ability was on cooldown, and the enemies were closing in. In a moment of panic, Zappo accidentally used the Succubus's ability again, only to realize that it had a long cooldown. This led to a near-death experience, prompting Zappo to switch to a Voidwalker for tanking purposes. The Succubus's Seduction ability has a 2-minute cooldown, which might be why many Warlocks prefer the Voidwalker for reliability in combat situations.
◁/im_middle|> [end of text]


